  "version": 1,
  "description": "Per-step execution cost of every GitHub Actions job in ci.yml, and the ceiling on the two governance jobs combined. The object list is discovered by reading ci.yml together with qa-gate-surface.json — a step is in scope when it executes a ci-required gate — because a hand-listed set would guard exactly the steps that existed when it was written. Verified offline by scripts/qa/ci-cost.rb in the ci.yml governance job; refreshed from `gh run` locally with --refresh --write. Durations are compared against a threshold rather than for equality: a duration is a sample, not a function of the tree (FR-140, DD-153).",
  "workflow": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
  "budget": {
    "jobs": [
      "governance",
      "ci-environment-parity"
    ],
    "seconds": 2700,
    "decidedBy": "docs/design_doc/orchestrator/153-governance-execution-cost.md",
    "reason": "45 minutes for the two governance jobs combined. Not derived from the measured value, which FR-140 forbids: 45 minutes is the top of the range the whole pipeline occupied when FR-140 was filed (24-45 min end to end), so the line says governance alone may not cost what the entire pipeline used to. At the time it was set the pair measured 4798s, so it binds immediately and by a wide margin rather than ratifying the status quo.",
    "reviewWhen": "A new gate that does not fit is not a reason to raise this silently. Whoever adds it either makes room or raises the ceiling in this file with a written reason and a new date. Revisit unconditionally if the runner class changes, since the number assumes GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest."
  },
